te|8] someone [through|9] the mail.","根據達爾文獎記錄的一份廣為流傳的記載，一名名叫哈伊 · 拉赫納傑特的伊拉克恐怖分子曾設計了一種信件炸彈，意圖透過郵件刺殺某人。"],["His plan [demanded|10] [meticulous|11] [preparation|12]: the [explosive|13] had to survive the [postal system|14] and [detonate|15] only when the [intended|16] [recipient|17] opened the package.","他的計劃需要精心準備：爆炸物必須能夠經受住郵政系統的考驗，並且只有在收件人打開包裹時才會引爆。"],["Yet after [handling|18] the [complicated|19] task of [constructing|20] a [lethal|21] device, Rahnajet allegedly [overlooked|22] one [remarkably|23] simple detail — [postage|24].","然而，在完成了製造致命裝置的複雜任務後，拉赫納傑特據稱卻忽略了一個極其簡單的細節——郵資。"],["He had [inadvertently|25] [failed to|26] put [sufficient|27] postage on the package.","他無意中少貼了足夠的郵資。"],["[Instead of|28] reaching its intended [target|29], the lethal [parcel|30] was [rejected|31] by the postal service and [marked|32] “Return to Sender.”","這個致命包裹沒有送到預定目標手中，而是被郵局拒收，並被標記為「退回寄件人」。"]]},{"a":1,"h":"第 2 段","p":[["Since the package [contained|33] the sender's [information|34], it eventually made its way back [to|35] the very person who had [originally|36] [dispatched|37] it.","由於包裹上包含寄件人的信息，它最終回到了最初寄出包裹的人手中。"],["What happened next [transformed|38] an [attempted|39] [assassination|40] into a story of [extraordinary|41] [irony|42].","接下來發生的事情，將一起未遂的暗殺事件變成了一個充滿諷刺意味的故事。"],["When Rahnajet received the returned package, he [reportedly|43] failed to [recognize|44] — or simply forgot — that it [contained|45] the explosive device he [himself|46] had [assembled|47].","據報道，當拉納傑特收到退回的包裹時，他沒有意識到——或者只是忘記了——包裹裡裝著他自己組裝的爆炸裝置。"],["Without taking even the most basic [precautions|48], he opened it.","他連最基本的預防措施都沒採取，就打開了它。"],["The [device|49] [detonated|50], killing its maker rather than its intended victim.","裝置爆炸了，炸死了它的製造者，而不是它預定的目標。"],["The story later [became associated with|51] the Darwin Awards, which [are renowned for|52] [collecting|53] accounts of people whose [astonishingly|54] [foolish|55] decisions [result in|56] their own deaths.","這個故事後來與達爾文獎聯繫了起來。達爾文獎以收集那些因極其愚蠢的決定而喪命的人的故事而聞名。"]]},{"a":2,"h":"第 3 段","p":[["Few stories [illustrate|57] the concept more [vividly|58]: a man [supposedly|59] [possessed|60] enough [technical|61] [knowledge|62] to [construct|63] a deadly [explosive|64], [yet|65] [lacked|66] the [foresight|67] to pay the correct postage and then opened his own [bomb|68] when the postal [service|69] returned it.","很少有故事能比這更生動地詮釋這個概念：據說，一個男人擁有足夠的技術知識來製造致命的炸彈，卻因為缺乏遠見，忘記支付正確的郵資，結果在郵局退回包裹後，他自己打開了炸彈。"],["There is, however, an important [caveat|70]. The Darwin Awards [website|71] itself [classifies|72] the account as “[Unconfirmed|73] by Darwin.”","然而，這裡有一個重要的注意事項。達爾文獎的官方網站將這個故事列為「未經達爾文證實」。"],["In other words, although the story has [persisted|74] [for decades|75], there is [insufficient|76] [reliable|77] evidence to [corroborate|78] the claim that the [incident|79] [occurred|80] exactly [as described|81].","換句話說，儘管這個故事流傳了幾十年，但沒有足夠的可靠證據來證實事件確實如描述的那樣發生過。"],["Whether [historical|82] fact or [urban|83] [legend|84], its irony remains difficult to [surpass|85].","無論這是歷史事實還是都市傳說，其諷刺意味都難以超越。"]]}],"K":[[[[0.24,0],[0.7,0.118],[1.4,0.186],[2.71,0.305],[2.98,0.373],[3.55,0.491],[3.81,0.559],[4.32,0.678],[4.61,0.746],[4.92,0.814],[5.05,0.882],[5.43,1]],[[6.62,0],[7.12,0.051],[7.42,0.072],[7.55,0.093],[8.09,0.144],[8.79,0.211],[9.23,0.247],[9.69,0.299],[9.98,0.319],[10.21,0.34],[10.42,0.376],[11.32,0.412],[11.58,0.433],[12.16,0.484],[12.83,0.536],[13.28,0.556],[13.6,0.577],[14.4,0.629],[14.88,0.649],[15.34,0.685],[15.66,0.706],[16.26,0.742],[16.64,0.763],[17.25,0.814],[17.52,0.835],[18.31,0.902],[18.69,0.938],[18.88,0.959],[19.23,0.979],[19.36,1]],[[20.11,0],[20.34,0.025],[20.8,0.051],[21.37,0.114],[22.44,0.196],[23.66,0.278],[24.05,0.303],[24.62,0.367],[24.77,0.392],[25.01,0.418],[25.37,0.462],[25.48,0.487],[25.83,0.532],[26.64,0.576],[26.88,0.601],[27.49,0.664],[27.86,0.709],[27.96,0.734],[28.13,0.76],[28.66,0.823],[29.05,0.886],[29.63,0.93],[29.81,0.956],[30.29,1]],[[31.23,0],[31.74,0.028],[32.23,0.078],[32.76,0.127],[33.08,0.155],[33.91,0.247],[34.24,0.275],